First, how about we go over the rules, shall we?

153
00:08:10,508 --> 00:08:12,808
ルール！
Rules!

154
00:08:11,808 --> 00:08:14,308
ルール説明をしてくださるそうです。
Sounds like they're going to explain the rules.

155
00:08:13,608 --> 00:08:15,508
はい！
Yes!

156
00:08:14,508 --> 00:08:16,508
Yes, how are you doing, everyone? Okay.

157
00:08:16,008 --> 00:08:18,508
わしの英語も試されますね。
My English is going to be tested too.

158
00:08:16,508 --> 00:08:22,508
So let's review the rules and learn a little bit about Jump King while we are at it, you guys, okay?

159
00:08:21,008 --> 00:08:22,508
はい！
Yes!

160
00:08:22,508 --> 00:08:28,508
Um, so, in case those of you who don't know anything about Jump King or are in attendance...

161
00:08:27,208 --> 00:08:30,008
何も知らない人が…
For people who don't know anything...

162
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:31,008
Let's teach you guys a little bit about it.

163
00:08:30,208 --> 00:08:33,208
改めて説明してくださるのじゃ。
they're explaining it for us once more.

164
00:08:31,008 --> 00:08:44,008
So first of all, Jump King is a difficult 2D platformer game where the player must climb a tall tower. It is infamous for its difficulty as you cannot change the direction of your jump once you have pressed the jump button. Very, very difficult game, especially for that...

165
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:41,508
勝利の…高い塔を登る…
For victory... climbing a tall tower...

166
00:08:42,508 --> 00:08:45,008
ジャンプボタンを…
The jump button...

167
00:08:46,508 --> 00:08:48,808
ジャンプボタンをね、押す難しいゲーム。
It's a hard game where you press the jump button.

168
00:08:48,808 --> 00:08:54,008
And also the amount of time you hold the jump button affects the power of the jump.

169
00:08:49,008 --> 00:08:54,508
なんか押す強さとかでジャンプできる高さが違うらしいのじゃ。
Like, the height of your jump varies depending on how long you press it.

170
00:08:54,508 --> 00:08:58,008
すみません、変な日本語が入ってるかもしれないけど、お願います！
Sorry, there might be some weird Japanese in here, but please go ahead!

171
00:08:56,508 --> 00:08:59,008
はい、全然！読みますね。
No problem at all! I'll read it.

172
00:08:59,008 --> 00:09:06,008
「Jump King」は、プレイヤーが高い塔を登らなければならない難易度の高い2Dプラットフォーマーゲームです。
"Jump King is a challenging 2D platformer game where players must climb a tall tower."

173
00:09:06,008 --> 00:09:14,008
ジャンプボタンを押すとジャンプの方向を変更できなくなるため、その難易度の高い、悪名高いゲームとなっております。
"Once you press the jump button, you can't change directions mid-air, making it a notoriously difficult game."

174
00:09:14,008 --> 00:09:16,008
ドむずゲームじゃ！
It's a super-duper hard game!

175
00:09:14,808 --> 00:09:20,508
ジャンプボタンを長押しする時間によってジャンプの勢いが変わるようになっております！
"The strength of your jump changes depending on how long you hold down the jump button!"

176
00:09:20,008 --> 00:09:23,008
時間によって変わるらしいのじゃ！
It changes based on the timing!

177
00:09:21,008 --> 00:09:25,508
Yes, it is difficult game, very hard.
Yes, it is a difficult game, very hard.

178
00:09:25,008 --> 00:09:26,508
むずむずゲーム。
A super hard game.

179
00:09:26,008 --> 00:09:33,208
いや、本当に難しい！時間でね、ぴょんとか小ジャンプとか中ジャンプとかね、そういうのがありますね。
It really is hard! Depending on the duration, there are little hops, short jumps, medium jumps, and things like that.

180
00:09:30,808 --> 00:09:35,808
わしがさっき練習したやつじゃの！あちちで使い分けてたやつじゃの！
That's what I was practicing earlier! That's what I was alternating!

181
00:09:33,508 --> 00:09:38,208
Yes, very difficult! But today...

182
00:09:37,008 --> 00:09:38,808
うん、とっても難しい。
Yeah, really difficult.

183
00:09:38,208 --> 00:09:45,008
We have very specific rules for this, for this race. It's not really a tournament, it's a race.

184
00:09:39,008 --> 00:09:41,208
しかし！
However!

185
00:09:41,208 --> 00:09:42,808
ルールが…
The rules are...

186
00:09:43,008 --> 00:09:44,808
このレースでは？
In this race?

187
00:09:45,008 --> 00:09:51,508
All racers will start at the very bottom of the map, with their timers set to 00:00:00,

188
00:09:47,808 --> 00:09:51,208
一番最初からスタート！
Starting from the very beginning!

189
00:09:51,208 --> 00:09:55,208
0秒から1時間スタートのところで、
Starting from zero seconds for one hour,

190
00:09:51,508 --> 00:09:59,008
until the timer hits one hour. Our racers will need to jump as high as they possibly can. However, it is easy to fall down very far,

191
00:09:54,008 --> 00:09:56,508
登り始めて、
start climbing,

192
00:09:56,008 --> 00:09:58,508
どこまで行けるか…
and see how far they can get...

193
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:04,016
...to adapt. I know some of them have been practicing, and some have not, which will make it even...

194
00:10:03,916 --> 00:10:08,366
練習してる人もいれば、しない人もいる大会ですよという事ですのじゃ。
So it's a tournament where some people have practiced and some haven't, noja.

195
00:10:08,516 --> 00:10:15,516
え、すべてのレーサーはマップの最下部からスタートし、タイマーは00:00:00...
All racers will start at the bottom of the map, with the timer set to 00:00:00...

196
00:10:13,516 --> 00:10:15,816
0にね。最初から。
To zero, right. Right from the beginning.

197
00:10:16,016 --> 00:10:22,516
タイマーが1時間になるまでに、レーサーたちはできるだけ高くジャンプしなければなりません。
Racers must jump as high as possible before the timer reaches one hour.

198
00:10:20,816 --> 00:10:22,816
できるだけ高く。
As high as possible.

199
00:10:22,616 --> 00:10:26,516
だからクリア1回っていうよりは、どこまで行けるかなみたいな...
So rather than trying to clear it once, it's more about how far you can get...

200
00:10:23,016 --> 00:10:29,816
しかしあっという間に下まで落ちてしまうこともあるので、状況に応じて対応していく必要があります。
However, since you can fall all the way back down in the blink of an eye, you'll need to adapt to the situation.

201
00:10:28,016 --> 00:10:33,516
多分、1時間後の現在地ってことじゃな？最高地点というよりも。
So it probably goes by your current position at the one-hour mark, right? Rather than your highest point.

202
00:10:33,816 --> 00:10:36,016
そうだね、ちょっとギャンブルね。
Exactly, it's a bit of a gamble.

203
00:10:35,216 --> 00:10:37,516
そう、1時間の近くになって...
Yeah, once it gets close to the one-hour mark...

204
00:10:36,816 --> 00:10:40,816
ジャンプしていくか、それとも止まっておくかみたいなのも...
Whether to keep jumping or stay put...

205
00:10:40,516 --> 00:10:44,616
結構3位に入るには考えなきゃいけないのかなと...
...is something you really need to consider to make the top three.

206
00:10:43,816 --> 00:10:48,516
確かに。「ここまで行けたからもういいか」って止まって雑談したっていいわけじゃろ？
Good point. You could just say, "I made it this far, so I'm good," stop, and just chat, right?

207
00:10:46,516 --> 00:10:48,816
どこで止まるか考えてみてください。
Please consider where to stop.

208
00:10:48,516 --> 00:10:51,516
それも含めて計算らしいでのじゃ。
Figuring that out is part of the strategy too, noja.

209
00:10:49,816 --> 00:10:52,816
最後の10分がちょっと怖いかもね。
Those final 10 minutes might be pretty nerve-wracking.

210
00:10:52,016 --> 00:10:56,516
「最後の10分で落下しちゃった」みたいなことも全然あるわけじゃしね。意味ないですので。
After all, someone could easily end up falling in the last 10 minutes. That would ruin everything.

211
00:10:56,716 --> 00:10:58,716
そう、ギャンブルじゃん！
Exactly, it's a total gamble!

212
00:10:58,016 --> 00:11:02,016
そう、ギャンブル！本当にギャンブルですな。大会らしいですのじゃ。
Yeah, a gamble! It really is a gamble. Just what you'd expect from a tournament, noja.

213
00:11:02,216 --> 00:11:04,216
気をつけてね、みんな。
Be careful, everyone.

214
00:11:03,016 --> 00:11:05,216
戦略が必要じゃ。
You need a strategy.

215
00:11:04,816 --> 00:11:18,016
So when time is up, racers will take a screenshot of their last position. We'll use that screenshot to decide who has officially climbed the farthest up the tower. Please note: it's okay if the timer has run a bit further than one hour as long as the contestant has stopped moving at 01:00:00.

216
00:11:09,016 --> 00:11:12,316
レースが終わったらスクリーンショット撮ってくださいと。
Once the race is over, take a screenshot.

217
00:11:18,216 --> 00:11:25,016
タイマー自体はいいけど、1時間00になったら動くのはやめてくださいと。
The timer itself can run over, but stop moving once it hits 1:00:00.

218
00:11:18,016 --> 00:11:28,516
I know sometimes you're excited you jump a little bit extra, but stop moving at one hour, and then you you can take your screenshot. As long as they stopped moving one hour in, it's totally fine. All right.

219
00:11:28,516 --> 00:11:34,516
はい。制限時間が終了したら、参加者は最後の位置のスクリーンショットを撮って提出していただきます。
Right. Once the time limit is up, participants will take and submit a screenshot of their final position.

220
00:11:33,016 --> 00:11:36,216
ラスト10分雑談でいいか。できるだけ高く登る。
Guess I can just chat for the last 10 minutes. Climb as high as you can.

221
00:11:34,816 --> 00:11:40,816
このスクリーンショットを元に、塔を最も高く登り切った参加者を正式に決定します。
Based on this screenshot, we will officially determine who has climbed the highest up the tower.

222
00:11:41,016 --> 00:11:48,016
1時間の時点で参加者が動きを止めている限り、タイマーが1時間を少し超えていても問題ないですので...
As long as the participant stops moving at the one-hour mark, it's fine if the timer slightly exceeds one hour...

223
00:11:42,516 --> 00:11:45,016
勝ち確ステージだったら雑談するか。
If I'm in a winning spot, maybe I'll just chat.

224
00:11:47,816 --> 00:11:51,816
Go or stay. そう、選ばれしお前たち。
Go or stay. That's right, chosen ones.

225
00:11:48,016 --> 00:11:54,016
1時間経った時にピタッと止まっていただけると嬉しいです。そこをスクリーンショットして送ってください。
...so we'd appreciate it if you stop completely at the one-hour mark. Please take a screenshot there and send it in.

226
00:11:54,016 --> 00:11:57,016
はい、スクリーンショットして送ってくださいとのこと。
Okay, so take a screenshot and send it in.

227
00:11:57,016 --> 00:12:00,616
あ、主ら！今のうちにわしの動画、高評価してくれたら嬉しいのじゃ〜！
Ah, viewers! While we have time, I'd really appreciate it if you'd drop a like on my stream, noja!

228
00:12:00,516 --> 00:12:12,516
Completion of the game is not required, nor is it likely, but in the event a racer completes the game, they will start a new game right away upon reaching the babe at the top, and continue climbing once again until the timer hits 01:00:00.

229
00:12:03,016 --> 00:12:05,016
頑張れ〜！あちちめら〜！
Do your best! Achichi Mela!

230
00:12:07,516 --> 00:12:11,016
吹っ飛ばされても落ちても愛してね、主ら！
Love me even if I get blown away or fall, okay, viewers?!

231
00:12:12,516 --> 00:12:26,516
Again, it's unlikely, you know, this is just for newbies and, you know, I didn't want to put them through 2 hours of racing, or even three. I think one is enough to get the general idea of how they're doing, but...

232
00:12:26,516 --> 00:12:30,016
...yes, if someone does complete it, they will have to start again.

233
00:12:30,216 --> 00:12:37,016
ゲームをクリアする必要はなく、そもそもクリアできる可能性はとても低いですが...
Completing the game is not required, and the chances of clearing it are very low to begin with, but...

234
00:12:32,016 --> 00:12:36,516
クリアは... クリアできるやつおるんかな？だ、だって初心者大会だからね？
Clearing it... Is there anyone who actually could? I mean, this is a beginner tournament, right?

235
00:12:37,016 --> 00:12:38,216
万が一ね。
Just in case.

236
00:12:37,216 --> 00:12:46,016
万が一レーサーがゲームをクリアした場合は、頂上の美女に到達するとすぐに新しいゲームを開始し、タイマーが1時間になるまで再度登り続けてください。
In the unlikely event a racer clears the game, as soon as they reach the babe at the top, please start a new game and keep climbing until the timer hits one hour.

237
00:12:38,516 --> 00:12:40,516
万が一クリアした場合は？
In the unlikely event someone clears it?

238
00:12:43,016 --> 00:12:45,516
あ、2周目もOKです。
Ah, a second loop is okay.

239
00:12:46,216 --> 00:12:49,816
2周目もOKらしいでのじゃ。クリアできたらいいらしい。
Sounds like a second lap is okay, noja. If you manage to clear it, that is.

240
00:12:49,816 --> 00:12:55,816
でもお主、先、すっごい頑張ったのに1時間。あの、5%しか進んでなかったんじゃが？
But hey, I tried so hard earlier for an hour... and only made 5% progress, you know?!

241
00:12:55,516 --> 00:12:59,816
低いですけど、まあ奇跡が起こるかもしれませんからね。
The chances are slim, but a miracle might happen after all.

242
00:12:59,016 --> 00:13:01,016
奇跡が起こるかも！
Maybe a miracle will happen!

243
00:13:00,816 --> 00:13:10,516
Just in case, right? Now all of today's racers are brand-new racers, and they have only had 5 days to practice. We will start the race when Mori says "Go!".

244
00:13:08,516 --> 00:13:16,816
確かに。告知されてから、結構「練習OKです」みたいな感じじゃったから...
True. Since the announcement, it was pretty much like, "Go ahead and practice"...

245
00:13:10,516 --> 00:13:17,816
The top 3 jumpers will receive prizes! May the next Jump King emerge victorious! Yes! Please!

246
00:13:17,816 --> 00:13:22,016
まだ練習期間が5日しか与えられておりません。
They've only been given a 5-day practice period.

247
00:13:18,016 --> 00:13:25,816
今日の出場者は全員初めてレースに参加する選手たちで、練習期間はわずか5日間しかありませんでした。
Today's participants are all racers competing for the first time, and the practice period was only five days.

248
00:13:23,516 --> 00:13:26,016
わし昨日からしかやってない。
I only started yesterday.

249
00:13:26,016 --> 00:13:30,816
カリオペ先輩が「ゴー！」と合図を出したらレースを開始します。
When Calliope-senpai gives the signal "Go!", the race will begin.

250
00:13:27,516 --> 00:13:32,516
これ今あれだな。テスト勉強してないみたいな言ってる人みたいになってる。
Now I sound like one of those people who says they didn't study for the test.

251
00:13:31,516 --> 00:13:35,016
上位3名のジャンパーには豪華な賞品が贈られます。
The top three jumpers will receive luxurious prizes.

252
00:13:34,516 --> 00:13:39,016
頑張ります！今日朝まで練習したのじゃ！
I'll do my best! I practiced until this morning, noja!

253
00:13:35,016 --> 00:13:40,016
新たな「ジャンプキング」の伝説の幕開けを楽しみにしておりますー！
We're looking forward to the dawn of a new Jump King legend!

254
00:13:40,516 --> 00:13:46,516
いやー、賞品！豪華賞品がもらえる！豪華賞品いただいてもよろしいか？
Wow, prizes! We get luxurious prizes! Would it be alright if I took one home?

255
00:13:41,516 --> 00:13:48,016
はい。楽しみですね。ジャンプキングを愛する皆さんにとっても楽しみ...
Yes. So exciting. Exciting for all Jump King lovers too...

256
00:13:47,516 --> 00:13:49,816
欲しいのじゃ〜！
I want one, noja~!

257
00:13:49,016 --> 00:13:52,516
そうだね。何にしてあげようかな？
That's right. Wonder what we should give them?

258
00:13:50,016 --> 00:13:54,016
実際何貰えるんだろう？トロフィーとかかな？
What do we actually get? A trophy or something?

259
00:13:53,016 --> 00:13:59,016
Now before we get started, we have a special message to share with all of you guys today.

260
00:13:55,516 --> 00:13:58,016
スペシャルメッセージ？
Special message?

261
00:13:59,016 --> 00:14:04,516
First though, I will go ahead and let the racers know we will actually probably go ahead and start at 20.

262
00:14:04,016 --> 00:14:07,516
20？20分から？
20? At 20 past?

263
00:14:04,516 --> 00:14:10,516
So just a moment please while I send everybody the message. 19:20.

264
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:17,016
はい、7時20分よりレース始める感じになる気がしますのじゃ。
All right, looks like the race will be starting at 7:20, noja.

265
00:14:17,016 --> 00:14:21,016
So, はい、20 will start. 特別なメッセージありますよ。
So, yes, we will start at 20. We have a special message!

266
00:14:21,016 --> 00:14:23,016
特別なメッセージですか？
A special message?

267
00:14:22,516 --> 00:14:24,016
そうだよ。
That's right.

268
00:14:23,516 --> 00:14:27,016
どなたでしょうか？前世の... あ、伝説の方ですか？
Who could it be? From a past li... Ah, a legendary figure?

269
00:14:26,016 --> 00:14:30,016
伝説の方からメッセージもらいました。
We received a message from a legend.

270
00:14:27,516 --> 00:14:30,016
おお！伝説？！
Ooh! A legend?!

271
00:14:29,516 --> 00:14:36,516
We received a very special message, everyone, from the Jump King! From the Jump King herself!

272
00:14:36,516 --> 00:14:41,216
So the Jump King has a message for all of today's racers! Jajan!
So the Jump King has a message for all of today's racers! Ta-da!

273
00:14:41,516 --> 00:14:43,216
ジャジャン！
Ta-da!

274
00:14:42,516 --> 00:14:44,016
おお！
Ooh!

275
00:14:43,816 --> 00:14:45,516
ジャンプキング！
The Jump King!

276
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:48,816
ホロレースに参加の皆さん、お疲れ様です！
To everyone participating in the HoloRace, thank you for your hard work!

277
00:14:45,016 --> 00:14:46,516
いろは先輩！
Iroha-senpai!

278
00:14:47,016 --> 00:14:48,516
お疲れ様です！
Good work!

279
00:14:48,516 --> 00:14:50,016
風真いろはです！
It's Kazama Iroha!

280
00:14:49,516 --> 00:14:52,016
おお、ジャンプキングのマスター！
Ooh, the Jump King master!

281
00:14:51,816 --> 00:14:57,816
本日、ジャンプキングを愛する者として、RTA勢の皆さんに...
Today, as a lover of Jump King, to everyone running this speedrun...

282
00:14:54,016 --> 00:14:56,516
めっちゃ上手い。RTA勢。
She's super good. Speedrunners.

283
00:14:57,216 --> 00:15:00,040
...アドバイスをしに来ました！
...I've come to offer some advice!

284
00:14:58,016 --> 00:15:00,040
え、アドバイスきた！きたきたきた！
Eh, we're getting advice! Here it comes, here it comes!

285
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:01,824
...I'll give you some advice.

286
00:15:01,924 --> 00:15:04,824
このゲームのポイントはですね、
The key to this game is...

287
00:15:04,924 --> 00:15:05,624
はい。
Yes.

288
00:15:05,724 --> 00:15:07,524
そう、Chill。
That's right, chill.

289
00:15:07,624 --> 00:15:08,524
Chill？え？
Chill? What?

290
00:15:08,424 --> 00:15:09,624
まあまあまあ、確かにね。
Well, well, true enough.

291
00:15:09,624 --> 00:15:13,024
今日いろは先輩の朝配信ちょっと見したけど、
I tuned in a bit to Iroha-senpai's morning stream today, but...

292
00:15:10,224 --> 00:15:12,324
それさえ覚えておけばいい！
All you need to remember is that!

293
00:15:13,024 --> 00:15:15,524
「Chill」って言いながら落ちたのじゃん。
she kept falling while saying "chill."

294
00:15:14,524 --> 00:15:16,224
忘れないことが大事。
Not forgetting that is what's important.

295
00:15:15,824 --> 00:15:16,724
確かに。
True.

296
00:15:16,724 --> 00:15:20,524
So, the key to this game is chill. Yes, chill.

297
00:15:20,224 --> 00:15:21,424
Chillだって。
"Chill," she says.

298
00:15:21,024 --> 00:15:26,524
If you fall, just climb back up. This might sound simple, but it is very important.

299
00:15:23,024 --> 00:15:26,024
初心者にChill精神あるのかな？
Do beginners even have that chill mindset?

300
00:15:26,224 --> 00:15:27,224
Wow...

301
00:15:27,224 --> 00:15:28,024
う〜ん。
Hmm.

302
00:15:27,824 --> 00:15:30,224
ジャンプキング、とても難しいですが、
Jump King is very difficult, but...

303
00:15:28,124 --> 00:15:30,824
上手い人がChillしながらやるのはあれじゃけど...
It's one thing for skilled players to stay chill...

304
00:15:30,324 --> 00:15:34,024
最後まであきらめず、全力で楽しんでください！応援してます！
don't give up until the very end, and enjoy it with all your might! I'm rooting for you!

305
00:15:33,824 --> 00:15:36,524
ありがとうなのじゃ〜！頑張るのじゃ〜！
Thank you so much-noja! I'll do my best-noja!

306
00:15:35,824 --> 00:15:37,324
That's our Jump King!

307
00:15:37,324 --> 00:15:38,224
Chill？
Chill?

308
00:15:38,324 --> 00:15:41,524
それでは皆さん、グッドラックでござる〜！
Well then, everyone, best of luck de gozaru~!

309
00:15:41,024 --> 00:15:43,024
ござる〜！
Gozaru~!

310
00:15:43,024 --> 00:15:44,524
初心者のChill...
A beginner staying chill...

311
00:15:44,324 --> 00:15:46,024
さすがね〜！
As expected!

312
00:15:46,024 --> 00:15:49,024
重みのある言葉、素晴らしいお言葉でしたね。
Such weighty words. That was wonderful advice.

313
00:15:49,024 --> 00:15:52,224
さすがジャンプキング、ありがとうございました！
Truly our Jump King, thank you so much!

314
00:15:52,024 --> 00:15:55,224
キーボード壊れんかったっけ？いろは先輩。気のせいかの？
Didn't Iroha-senpai break her keyboard? Or was that just my imagination?

315
00:15:54,024 --> 00:15:56,224
本当のジャンプキングだね。
A true Jump King, indeed.

316
00:15:55,424 --> 00:15:59,224
Chill... Chillでキーボード壊れるかの？本当にアドバイスはChillなのか？
Chill... Can a keyboard break when you're chill? Is the advice really to be chill?

317
00:15:58,824 --> 00:16:02,024
いろはちゃん、本当にありがとうね。優しい言葉...
Iroha-chan, thank you so much. Such kind words...

318
00:16:01,824 --> 00:16:04,524
やっぱキーボード壊すことから始まらない気がしてきたのじゃが。
I feel like you have to start by breaking your keyboard.

319
00:16:03,224 --> 00:16:06,624
...hardest advice they can get, so thank you so much.

320
00:16:06,524 --> 00:16:07,424
はい。
Yes.

321
00:16:07,424 --> 00:16:14,524
Now then, it looks like it might it might be just about time to get right into it.

322
00:16:11,224 --> 00:16:16,824
じゃあタイマーと...
Okay, the timer and...

323
00:16:14,624 --> 00:16:18,824
Um, but let's see. We'll start at 20, shall we?

324
00:16:18,824 --> 00:16:21,024
はい、20分。
Right, 20.

325
00:16:19,424 --> 00:16:21,224
20分から。
From 20 past.

326
00:16:21,024 --> 00:16:25,024
あの、19... 19時20分ぐらい、はい、スタートします。
Um, 19... around 19:20, yes, we will start.

327
00:16:23,224 --> 00:16:24,424
うん、後で。
Yeah, soon.

328
00:16:25,024 --> 00:16:27,224
え、じゃあもうすぐスタートなんじゃない？
Wait, so it's starting super soon then?

329
00:16:27,024 --> 00:16:29,624
はい、よろしくお願いします！
Yes, best of luck everyone!

330
00:16:28,224 --> 00:16:29,824
準備してくださーい。
Please get ready.

331
00:16:29,424 --> 00:16:31,524
はーい！頑張りますのじゃ！
Okay! I'll do my best-noja!

332
00:16:31,124 --> 00:16:33,024
いや、本当に楽しみだ、マジで。
Man, I'm really looking forward to this, honestly.

333
00:16:33,024 --> 00:16:35,024
う〜、ドキドキワクワクですね！
Ooh, it's so exciting and nerve-wracking!

334
00:16:34,824 --> 00:16:36,024
行けるかな〜？
Can I do this, I wonder?

335
00:16:35,824 --> 00:16:37,424
えー、どうなるかな〜？
Man, I wonder how it'll go?

336
00:16:37,024 --> 00:16:43,024
あの〜、同期の配信は見てて、今日のこと、そぴあの配信はちらっと見たんじゃけど、
Um, I've watched my genmates' streams, like I peeked at Sopia's stream today, but...

337
00:16:38,224 --> 00:16:42,524
いや〜、やっぱり色々...ね、結局落ちやすいんで...
Well, there's a lot... after all, it's so easy to fall...

338
00:16:43,024 --> 00:16:48,524
「うわ〜」ってなっても、そう、1回こう落ち着いてやるのが大事な気がしますね。
Even when you go "Aaargh!", taking a moment to calm down is so important.

339
00:16:44,224 --> 00:16:49,824
その他の参加者の先輩方の配信は、やっぱ敵じゃから、
As for the other participating senpais' streams, since they're the competition,

340
00:16:49,824 --> 00:16:53,024
やっぱ敵のを見るのって良くないかな〜みたいな。
I wondered if it's bad to scout out the competition, you know.

341
00:16:50,024 --> 00:16:52,424
前の様子も見たいですよね〜。
You want to see how it's looking ahead, though.

342
00:16:52,424 --> 00:16:54,024
答えを見ちゃう...
You'd see the answers...

343
00:16:53,224 --> 00:16:57,424
ちょっと良くないかな〜と思って見ないようにしていて、
I thought that might be somewhat unfair, so I avoided watching them,

344
00:16:57,424 --> 00:17:01,024
じゃから、あの、実際他の先輩がどれぐらいできるかとか...
and so, how well the other senpais can actually play...

345
00:17:00,824 --> 00:17:02,424
ちなみに、Rionaちゃん...
By the way, Riona-chan...

346
00:17:01,824 --> 00:17:06,024
そぴあとキョーコがどれぐらいできるかは大体分かってるんじゃけど、
While I generally know how well Sopia and Kyoko can play,

347
00:17:04,024 --> 00:17:08,524
そうですね、いろはのアドバイス、キーボードクラッシャーになれ、って言ってたんで...
Yeah, Iroha's advice was basically "become a keyboard crusher," so...

348
00:17:06,024 --> 00:17:08,424
他の方がどれぐらいできるかを分かっておらず、
I don't know how well the others do,

349
00:17:08,424 --> 00:17:11,424
どれぐらい行けるかな？
so I wonder how high I can reach?

350
00:17:08,424 --> 00:17:14,624
確かに長時間やってるとイライラしてくる可能性はあるんですけど、1時間だったらとにかく早く上がる！
Sure, if you play for hours you might get frustrated, but in one hour, just climb fast!

351
00:17:14,624 --> 00:17:16,824
早く！早く上がる！
Fast! Climb fast!

352
00:17:16,024 --> 00:17:18,024
早く上がる！当たり前で笑った！
Climb fast! That's so obvious, it made me laugh!

353
00:17:18,024 --> 00:17:19,024
落ち着いて！
Stay calm!

354
00:17:18,824 --> 00:17:21,024
落ち着いて早く上がる！理想じゃ！
Stay calm and climb fast! The ideal strategy!

355
00:17:20,524 --> 00:17:28,524
あとは覚えゲーだと思うので、ここは大ジャンプだったかな、中ジャンプだったかな、みたいなのをできるだけ覚えておくといいかもしれませんね。
Also, since it's a memorization game, remembering whether a spot needs a big jump or medium jump will really help.

356
00:17:29,024 --> 00:17:33,424
あれ、大ジャンプは「甘酒らんど」で、中ジャンプは「あちちめ...」で、
Wait, a big jump is "Amazake Land", a medium jump is "Achichime...",

357
00:17:32,424 --> 00:17:36,824
どれぐらいできるかな？練習の時間あんまりなかったかな？
I wonder how they'll do? They didn't have much practice time, right?

358
00:17:33,424 --> 00:17:35,424
小ジャンプは「あちっ」、じゃよな？
and a small jump is "Achi!", right?

359
00:17:37,024 --> 00:17:40,824
いや、そうですよね。何回もやるしかないですからね、ジャンプキングは。
Yeah, exactly. In Jump King, you just have to do it over and over.

360
00:17:40,424 --> 00:17:46,824
何回もやるしかない。いや、そう何回もやるしかない覚えゲーのジャンプキングにおいて、正直昨日から始めたというのはかなり不利なんじゃが、
"Just have to do it over and over." In a memorization game like Jump King where repetition is key, honestly having only started yesterday puts me at a huge disadvantage,

361
00:17:46,524 --> 00:17:50,024
みんなのVCを聞きに行く時間もあるし...
Plus we'll have time to drop into everyone's VC...

362
00:17:50,024 --> 00:17:54,824
不利ではありますが...頑張りますのじゃ！
disadvantage or not... I'll do my absolute best-noja!

363
00:17:51,824 --> 00:17:53,424
楽しみ、みんなの様子。
Looking forward to seeing everyone.

364
00:17:53,224 --> 00:17:55,024
頑張れ〜！
Go for it~!

365
00:17:55,024 --> 00:17:58,224
そうしますね。ちょっと邪魔しますね、私たち。
We'll do that. We'll be popping in to bother you a bit.

366
00:17:58,524 --> 00:18:00,224
お邪魔します。
We'll drop in.

367
00:17:59,824 --> 00:18:05,024
そう、入りに来てくださるらしい！お喋りに来てくださるらしいのじゃ！
Right, apparently they'll come visit! They'll come chat with us-noja!

368
00:18:01,824 --> 00:18:04,024
ぜひみんなの様子見せてください。
Please show us how you're doing.

369
00:18:05,024 --> 00:18:07,424
ちょっと意地悪、私たち。
We're a little mean, aren't we.

370
00:18:07,524 --> 00:18:09,024
そう。
Indeed.

371
00:18:08,524 --> 00:18:12,024
楽しみですね！ワクワクです。
Looking forward to it! So exciting.

372
00:18:12,524 --> 00:18:15,024
ちょっと集中するために...よいしょ。
Let me focus up a bit... heave-ho.

373
00:18:15,024 --> 00:18:17,024
あと2分です。
Two minutes left.

374
00:18:16,824 --> 00:18:18,524
皆さん、ドキドキ...
Everyone's heart is pounding...

375
00:18:18,524 --> 00:18:22,024
じゃあ、そろそろ先輩の配信を閉じ...閉じて、
Well then, it's about time I close... close Senpai's stream,

376
00:18:22,024 --> 00:18:26,024
えっとゲーム画面を開こうかの。
and open up the game screen.

377
00:18:22,024 --> 00:18:27,524
ボスになりたいから、今回はCalliope、アイアンマンみたいにOBSで...
I want to be like a boss, so this time Calliope, like Iron Man on OBS...

378
00:18:28,824 --> 00:18:30,824
よいしょ。
Heave-ho.

379
00:18:31,024 --> 00:18:33,224
これで閉じれたかの？
Did I manage to close it?

380
00:18:33,424 --> 00:18:36,024
んで、これで...
And then, with this...

381
00:18:36,424 --> 00:18:41,524
おぬしらにJump KingのBGM聞こえておるかの〜？どうじゃろうか？
Can you guys hear the Jump King BGM? How is it?

382
00:18:41,824 --> 00:18:45,024
どうじゃろうか？どうじゃろうか？良さそう？
How is it? How is it? Good?

383
00:18:45,524 --> 00:18:47,024
いい感じ？
Sounds okay?

384
00:18:47,824 --> 00:18:50,024
いい感じかの？
Is it sounding all right?

385
00:18:51,524 --> 00:18:54,024
聞こえる？オッケー、ありがとうなのじゃ！
You can hear it? Okay, thank you-noja!

386
00:18:54,024 --> 00:18:59,024
それでは、え〜これからは、え〜先輩が、あの「GO」という合図で
Now then, from here on, once Senpai gives the "GO" signal,

387
00:18:59,024 --> 00:19:02,524
始めていいらしいので、
we're allowed to start, so...

388
00:19:03,524 --> 00:19:06,024
え〜っと、どこじゃろうか？ここか。
Umm, where is it? Here?

389
00:19:06,824 --> 00:19:08,024
え〜っと...
Umm...

390
00:19:08,024 --> 00:19:10,524
「Hi!」こぼ先輩？！
"Hi!" Kobo-senpai?!

391
00:19:10,824 --> 00:19:13,224
W-Why? This is Mela VC.

392
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:23,824
なんかこぼ先輩が...ちょ、配信に音乗せられなかったんじゃけど、
Kobo-senpai just... wait, I couldn't get her audio onto the stream, but...

393
00:19:23,824 --> 00:19:28,024
こぼ先輩が、あの、一瞬来て「Hi!」つって「Bye!」つって去ってった！
Kobo-senpai came in for a second, said "Hi!", then "Bye!" and left!

394
00:19:28,524 --> 00:19:32,024
間違えちゃったのかな？
Did she get the wrong room?

395
00:19:32,024 --> 00:19:35,024
間違えちゃったのかな？それとも...それとも...
Did she get the wrong room? Or maybe... or maybe...

396
00:19:35,224 --> 00:19:39,024
え、これ実は、こういうもの？大会ってこういうものなの？
Wait, is this how it's actually supposed to be? Is that how tournaments work?

397
00:19:39,224 --> 00:19:43,024
わしが、わしが勝手を分かっていなかっただけの可能性あり。
There's a chance I just didn't understand the protocol.

398
00:19:43,224 --> 00:19:47,024
わしにか？これわしか？これ言ったのわしか？
To me? Was that for me? Did she say that to me?

399
00:19:47,824 --> 00:19:50,524
挨拶してくださった？初絡みこれでいいんか？！
Did she greet me? Is this really my first interaction with her?!

400
00:19:50,524 --> 00:19:53,024
スタートきた！スタートきた、おぬしら！
Start is here! The start is here, guys!

401
00:19:53,024 --> 00:19:55,524
ちょちょちょちょ、え、て、敵の...
Wait-wait-wait, wait, is that...

402
00:19:55,524 --> 00:19:59,224
敵の集中力を乱す作戦かも、しかして！
Could that have been a tactic to disrupt the opponent's concentration?!

403
00:19:56,524 --> 00:20:00,024
[Text: "あのてっぺんには、ぴっちぴちのギャルがいるという…"]
[Text: "They say there's a smoking hot babe at the top..."]

404
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:01,832
[Text: "あのてっぺんには、ぴっちぴちのギャルがいるという..."]
[Text: "They say a smoking hot babe is at the top..."]

405
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:01,912
集中力を乱す作戦できたか？
Was that a plan to break my concentration?

406
00:20:02,132 --> 00:20:02,852
はい！
All right!

407
00:20:02,972 --> 00:20:04,282
ということで！
And with that!

408
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:05,182
えっと...
Um...

409
00:20:06,632 --> 00:20:09,552
はい、左上00:02、始めます！
Okay, it's 00:02 on the top left, let's start!

410
00:20:09,712 --> 00:20:14,682
始めますのじゃ。なんか集中力が早速、あの、乱されておりますけれども...
Starting now, noja. My concentration has already been totally thrown off, but...

411
00:20:15,532 --> 00:20:17,352
乱されておりますけれども、びっくりした！
Even though I'm rattled, that really surprised me!

412
00:20:15,532 --> 00:20:20,532
[Title: レッドクラウンの森]
[Title: Red Crown Woods]

413
00:20:17,432 --> 00:20:19,882
だって、だってだってだって！来るって聞いてなかったのじゃ！
I mean, I mean, I mean! I didn't hear anyone was coming, noja!

414
00:20:19,982 --> 00:20:22,052
そういうこと？そういうこと？
Is that what this is? Is that it?

415
00:20:22,152 --> 00:20:24,452
こぼ先輩...クレバーこぼ先輩ってこと？
Kobo-senpai... clever Kobo-senpai, is that it?!

416
00:20:24,552 --> 00:20:27,732
わしの集中力を...乱す作戦？
A scheme to... mess with my concentration?

417
00:20:27,832 --> 00:20:30,252
ちょ、今ね、あのかなり、かなり心拍数上がってる。
Wait, right now, my heart rate has gone up by a lot.

418
00:20:30,332 --> 00:20:33,432
だって、だって先輩と急に話せるなんて思わなかったのじゃもん！
I mean, I never imagined I'd suddenly be talking with a senpai, noja!

419
00:20:33,552 --> 00:20:34,252
行くか。
Here we go.

420
00:20:34,382 --> 00:20:35,112
あっち！
There!

421
00:20:35,832 --> 00:20:36,552
あっち！
There!

422
00:20:36,732 --> 00:20:38,832
ちょっとウィンドウの位置変えたいな。あっち！
I want to adjust the window position a bit. There!

423
00:20:39,132 --> 00:20:43,032
ちょっと調整させてね。よいしょ。ここでいいかな？ここでいいかな？
Let me adjust it slightly. Up we go. Is this good? Is this fine?

424
00:20:43,132 --> 00:20:46,432
よし、じゃあ行きますのじゃ。よいしょ、あちちめらー！
All right, off I go, noja. Up we go, Achichimela~!

425
00:20:46,882 --> 00:20:49,032
あいや、心乱されまくり...あっち！
Ah man, my mind is completely scrambled... There!

426
00:20:49,352 --> 00:20:50,852
よいしょ、よしよしよし。
Up we go, good, good, good.

427
00:20:51,382 --> 00:20:53,632
えっーと、あちちめらー！
Um, Achichimela~!

428
00:20:54,232 --> 00:20:55,232
あっちめ！
Over here!

429
00:20:55,732 --> 00:20:57,932
あっちめ！ちょっと足りなかったね。
Over here! Didn't charge quite enough.

430
00:20:58,232 --> 00:20:59,032
あっち！
There!

431
00:20:59,232 --> 00:21:00,032
あっち！
There!

432
00:21:00,432 --> 00:21:02,132
あちちめらー！
Achichimela~!

433
00:21:02,332 --> 00:21:04,232
あちちめらー！
Achichimela~!

434
00:21:04,732 --> 00:21:05,732
あっちめ！
Over here!

435
00:21:06,132 --> 00:21:07,432
あっちめ！
Over here!

436
00:21:07,532 --> 00:21:08,532
うん。
Yeah.

437
00:21:09,332 --> 00:21:12,732
いや、なんか緊張してきた...緊張してきた。
Man, I'm getting so nervous... So nervous.

438
00:21:12,832 --> 00:21:16,882
さっき、さっき全然さー、さっきのさー、練習配信では全然別に緊張はしてなかったんじゃけど...
Earlier, during the practice stream earlier, I wasn't feeling nervous at all, but...

439
00:21:18,932 --> 00:21:28,032
急になんか、あの、初めて話す...初めて話す先輩と急に話せたことにより緊張が発生してきました。行きますのじゃ。
Suddenly, um... by unexpectedly getting to talk with a senpai I'd never spoken to before, the nerves suddenly kicked in. Here I go, noja.

440
00:21:28,532 --> 00:21:29,532
あっち！
There!

441
00:21:29,832 --> 00:21:31,532
あっち！あ、ちょっと...
There! Ah, wait...

442
00:21:31,632 --> 00:21:35,332
ちょちょちょちょ...ちょちょちょちょちょ...
Wait, wait, wait, wait... Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait...

443
00:21:35,432 --> 00:21:38,832
やっぱあれ、こぼ先輩の作戦じゃろ絶対！
That had to be Kobo-senpai's strategy, for sure!

444
00:21:39,132 --> 00:21:40,832
あちちめらー！
Achichimela~!

445
00:21:41,132 --> 00:21:42,032
よいしょ。
Up we go.

446
00:21:42,232 --> 00:21:43,032
あっち！
There!

447
00:21:43,232 --> 00:21:44,232
あっち！
There!

448
00:21:44,732 --> 00:21:45,632
にょ！
Nyo!

449
00:21:46,032 --> 00:21:50,832
あちちめらー！ちょっちょ、なんか最初より下手じゃない、わし？わし、ちょちょちょちょ...
Achichimela~! Wait, wait, aren't I playing worse than at the start? Am I... wait, wait, wait, wait...

450
00:21:51,132 --> 00:21:56,532
落ち着くか。一旦落ち着くか。ちょ、精神攻撃めっちゃ効くタイプのサラマンダーでやばい。
Calm down. Let me calm down for a second. Wait, I'm the type of salamander that takes critical damage from mental attacks, this is bad.

451
00:21:56,632 --> 00:21:59,232
サラマンダーって精神攻撃低いんや。
Salamanders have low mental attack defense, huh.

452
00:21:59,332 --> 00:22:01,332
行くのじゃ、あちちめらー！
Here I go, noja! Achichimela~!

453
00:22:01,832 --> 00:22:05,132
ペース乱されまくりなのじゃ。あちちめらー！
My pace is totally thrown off, noja. Achichimela~!

454
00:22:05,232 --> 00:22:08,132
はいはいはいはいはいはい。あちちめらー！
Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay. Achichimela~!

455
00:22:08,232 --> 00:22:09,532
はいはいはい。
